9. Common Machine Learning algorithms
You don't need to master every algorithm today. First, understand what each one is used for.
Algorithm	Common use
Linear Regression	Predicting numerical values
Logistic Regression	Classification
Decision Tree	Classification and regression
Random Forest	Combining multiple decision trees
K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)	Predicting from nearby examples
K-Means	Grouping similar data points
Support Vector Machine (SVM)	Classification and regression
Naive Bayes	Probabilistic classification
Neural Networks	Learning complex patterns
For example, if you want to predict a student's marks, Linear Regression may be a reasonable starting point. If you want to predict pass or fail, Logistic Regression or a Decision Tree may be suitable.
The best algorithm depends on the dataset, task, and performance requirements.
