- model.fit(X, y) trains the model.
- model.predict([[6]]) predicts marks for six study hours.
The data here is deliberately simple to demonstrate the process. It is not a realistic model of actual exam performance.
11. Placement interview questions
Q1. What is Machine Learning?
Machine Learning is a branch of AI that enables computers to learn patterns from data and make predictions or decisions.
Q2. What is the difference between supervised and unsupervised learning?
Supervised learning uses labeled data, whereas unsupervised learning discovers patterns in data without supplied target labels.
Q3. What is the difference between classification and regression?
Classification predicts categories, while regression predicts numerical values.
Q4. What is overfitting?
Overfitting occurs when a model learns the training data too closely and fails to generalize well to unseen data.
Q5. Why do we split data into training and testing sets?
We train the model on one portion and evaluate it on separate data to estimate how well it performs on unseen examples.
Q6. What is the difference between an algorithm and a model?
An algorithm is the learning procedure. A model is the fitted result after training the algorithm on data.
